    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Chegg is a public company, traded as CHGG, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Santa Clara. Its site presents it as a source of homework help and study support, offering 24/7 assistance across 50+ subjects with step-by-step solutions and access to real experts. It says its solutions are shaped by student feedback and sold through Chegg Study and Chegg Study Pack subscriptions, which the site says include additional partner benefits at no cost to subscribers. The site also carries a copyright notice for Chegg Inc. covering 2003 to 2025.\n\nThe company's AI product on record is CheggMate, described as a study AI assistant for academic help. Notes held alongside it flag student data, content accuracy, and honor code implications as considerations for the product.\n\nThe site cites a survey fielded between Sept. 9 and Oct. 3, 2024 among a random sample of U.S. customers who used Chegg Study or Chegg Study Pack in Q2 2024 and Q3 2024, with a respondent base of 712 among approximately 1,039,954 invites, and says respondents were entered into a drawing to win 1 of 10 $300 e-gift cards.",
